    rdf:value "composition,  but I don’t think we succeeded very well. Finally, Placci in a burst of good-humour told us the famous Thomson-Paget “secret of aesthetics”. The discovery, like Newton’s apple, Watts’ tea-pot, etc., came by accident. A plasterer happened to be at work in the Capitol when Kit was looking at a certain statue there. She noticed that she enjoyed looking at it more while the plasterer was tapping than when he was not. The tapping heightened her enjoyment. Hence the way to enjoy statues and pictures was to tap while you were looking - to tap rhythmically. From this earth-shaking discovery they went on to augment the rhythmical tapping by a tune, and they soon came to the conclusion "^^xsd:string ;
